removed page scrolling. v2.2.0 put Hand History, Statistics and Bankroll beside the betting column for
half-screen use, gave the bead plate a fixed 10 x 10 box of 100 colour-only hands and renamed the two
table panels; v2.2.1 shrank the dots and corrected the fill order. v2.3.0 made PASS record the
table's result. v2.4.0 gave the Tie insurance its own stake.

v2.5.0 is OCR groundwork: a spot-check tool (app/tools/ocr_check.py) for judging a capture region,
an accuracy readout built from the audit log that refuses to flatter, a retired Gemini model id
replaced with gemini-3.8-flash, and a phantom "stop" event removed from the audit log.

IMPORTANT: the screen reader has still only been tested against synthetic images and a roulette
screenshot. It has never read the user's casino display, and no calibration region has been measured.
Do not treat OCR as working until a real screenshot of the table reads correctly.

